  "rationale": "The one home (SPEC_STANDARD 15.4) of every policy value that generated code reads: typed constants of one deterministic provider module, because the Factory data/code seam (SPEC_STANDARD 15.9) gives a generator an access signature and never a value, and an address in a note is not dereferenced (SPEC_STANDARD 15.3.1). The value is decided in the State 2 decision named by source_refs and is written here once; no rules or config address repeats it. A consumer that needs one exact entry receives a scalar constant, not a tuple index or a mapping key. The release ceilings of A26 are release-fixed thresholds, not environment settings, so they are constants here and installation.release_ceilings assembles the ReleaseCeilings record from them.",
